   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3773"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dharmakīrti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi grags pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos grags</persName><birth notBefore="0550-01-01">after 550</birth><death notAfter="0660-12-31">before 660</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6120</idno><idno type="APIS">3773</idno><note type="comment">The dates 600-660 were proposed in [C7GN3X2Q].&#13;
The mid-sixth century for his birth date was proposed in [KQVXHPVH].</note></person><person xml:id="person3780"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dharmottara</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos mchog</persName><birth notBefore="0740-01-01">after 740</birth><death notAfter="0800-12-31">before 800</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P9950</idno><idno type="APIS">3780</idno><note type="comment">Proposed approximate dates: 740-800, 751-782, 775-806 (see [AAIEJBMW]).</note></person><person xml:id="person3786"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྔོག་བློ་ལྡན་ཤེས་རབ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog lo tsA ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog lo rtsa ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog dge slong blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo ldan bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsha ba chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo ts+tsha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo ldan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ma hA</persName><birth notBefore="1059-01-01" notAfter="1059-12-31">1059</birth><death notBefore="1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2551</idno><idno type="APIS">3786</idno><note type="comment">See [BAQ9MH4T]: 193 for the main events of his life.&#13;
&#13;
Three manuscript editions of his writings and translations were deposited respectively in rNgog Blo ldan shes rab's tomb, in the monastery of gSang phu (probably in the main assembly hall), and in Drin las kyi sde (ID:4357) ([7FZ3B926]: 107).</note></person><person xml:id="person3892"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya paN+Di ta kun dga' rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ས་སྐྱ་པཎྜི་ཏ་ཀུན་དགའ་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya paṇḍita</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje sa paN</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs gter gangs can mkhas pa'i gtsug rgyan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa paN</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya lo tsA ba</persName><birth notBefore="1182-01-01" notAfter="1182-12-31">1182</birth><death notBefore="1251-01-01" notAfter="1251-12-31">1251</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1056</idno><idno type="APIS">3892</idno><note type="comment">See [8S7FDMCJ]: 107 for a list of his most important disciples.</note></person><person xml:id="person4017"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa' dz+nya na shrI</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བྱང་ཆུབ་སེམས་དཔའ་ཛྙ་ན་ཤྲཱི</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong ye shes dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi ye shes</persName><birth notAfter="1240-12-31">before 1240</birth><death notAfter="1350-12-31">before 1350</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3JT13457</idno><idno type="APIS">4017</idno><note type="comment">This scholar composed two works of epistemology in gSang phu (ID:6173) and was familiar with Sa skya paṇḍita (ID:3892)'s Tshad ma rigs gter (ID:5564) and Chu mig pa (ID:4018)'s commentary on the Pramāṇaviniścaya (ID:5290).</note></person><person xml:id="person4018"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chu mig pa seng ge dpal</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཆུ་མིག་པ་སེང་གེ་དཔལ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang chu mig pa seng ge dpal bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gsang phu ba seng ge dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chu mig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sing ha shri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyal ba'i sras po chu mig pa</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1220-12-31">after 1200 before 1220</birth><death notBefore="1270-01-01" notAfter="1280-12-31">after 1270 before 1280</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8407</idno><idno type="APIS">4018</idno></person><person xml:id="person4593"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">Anonymous</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨཱནོཉམོཨུས</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4593</idno></person><person xml:id="person5551"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">jñānaśrībhadra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ye shes dpal bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">kha che dz+nya na shrI</persName><birth notBefore="1000-01-01">after 1000</birth><death notAfter="1100-12-31">before 1100</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4CZ15186</idno><idno type="APIS">5551</idno><note type="comment">Approximate life dates: 11th century (see [AAIEJBMW]).</note></person><person xml:id="person5554"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">devendrabuddhi</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lha dbang blo</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lha'i dbang po blo gros</persName><birth notBefore="0600-01-01">after 600</birth><death notAfter="0700-12-31">before 700</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P9946</idno><idno type="APIS">5554</idno><note type="comment">Approximate dates: 630-690 (see [AAIEJBMW]).</note></person><person xml:id="person5565"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sgros</persName><birth notAfter="1250-12-31">before 1250</birth><sex value="M"/><idno type="APIS">5565</idno><note type="comment">Possibly an interpreter of Dharmakīrti, as the mention "sgros" appears three times, along with the name of Dharmottara (ID:3780), to identify the proponent of a view in a commentary on the Pramāṇaviniścaya (ID:3774) by Byang chub sems dpa' dz+nya na shrI (ID:4017). The proponents named in that work are usually Indian commentators, with the exception of "lo tswa ba" (rNgog blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786)).</note></person><person xml:id="person5566"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">Anonymous</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨཱནོཉམོཨུས</persName><birth notAfter="1200-12-31">before 1200</birth><death notAfter="1350-12-31">before 1350</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">5566</idno><note type="comment">Instructor (yongs 'dzin) of Dz+nya na shrI (ID:4017). Referred to once for his epistemological views in his pupil's commentary on the Pramāṇaviniścaya, work (ID:4769).</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3774"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pramāṇaviniścaya</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam nges</title><date type="composition" notBefore="0560-01-01" notAfter="0660-12-31">after 560 before 660</date><author ref="person:3773">dharmakīrti</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3774</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4767"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i snying po de kho na nyid bsdus pa gsal byed nyi ma'i 'od</title><title xml:lang="bo">རིགས་པའི་སྙིང་པོ་དེ་ཁོ་ན་ཉིད་བསྡུས་པ་གསལ་བྱེད་ཉི་མའི་འོད</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa'i de kho na nyid bsdus pa gsal byed nyi ma'i 'od</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa'i de kho na nyid gsal byed nyi ma'i 'od</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma mdo sde bdun 'grel pa 'grel bshad bcas pa'i snying po rigs pa'i de kho na nyid bsdus pa gsal byed nyi ma'i 'od</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa' dz+nyA na shri'i rigs pa'i snying po de kho na nyid bsdus pa gsal byed nyi ma'i 'od</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa snying po</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1260-01-01" notAfter="1380-12-31">after 1260 before 1380</date><author ref="person:4017">byang chub sems dpa' dz+nya na shrI</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The work is a compilation of definitions and typologies organized in 20 topics (which reminds one of the "lessons" in bsdus grwa compositions), which are the same as in work (ID:4773) by Sangs rgyas rgyal mtshan (ID:5910). See [J4L5X9AG]: 435.&#13;
Date of composition: drag po'i lo sa ga zla ba'i dkar phyogs. The waxing phase of the moon, in the "drag po" year: this indicates the 54th year of the cycle, which could correspond to 1260 - at the earliest, since the work cites the Tshad ma rigs gter (ID:5564) - 1320, or 1380 (probably not later).</note><idno type="APIS">4767</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4769"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam nges kyi TIk+ka blo gsal mgul rgyan</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་རྣམ་ངེས་ཀྱི་ཊཱིཀྐ་བློ་གསལ་མགུལ་རྒྱན</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad rnam par nges pa'i TIk+kka blo gsal gyi mgul</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1230-01-01">after 1230</date><author ref="person:4017">byang chub sems dpa' dz+nya na shrI</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Commentary on the three chapters of the Pramāṇaviniścaya, abundantly using "thal...phyir" arguments. It is possibly incomplete - it ends abruptly, but has a colophon.&#13;
Contains numerous references to Indian commentators of the Pramāṇaviniścaya (ID:3774), Pramāṇavārttika (ID:3772) and Pramāṇasamuccaya (ID:3770), as well as to the views of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786), of Chu mig pa (ID:4018), and to the Tshad ma rigs gter (ID:5564).&#13;
